# Next.js & React

## Client vs server

- Add `'use client'` only when using hooks, browser APIs, Redux, or event handlers in that file
- Server actions: `'use server'` at top of action files (e.g. `src/features/**/actions/*.ts`, `src/app/actions.ts`)
- Keep data fetching in services, hooks, or server actions—not duplicated in presentational components

## Components

- Functional components; default export for pages and main component files
- Colocate feature UI under `src/features/<feature>/components/`
- Wrap fragile UI with existing `ErrorBoundary` from `@/common/ErrorBoundry` where the app already does
- Toasts: use `useToast` + `ToastContainer` pattern from `@/components/Toasts/`

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes; follow existing spacing and dark/light patterns from `ThemeContext`
- Arabic copy and RTL-friendly layouts appear in product UI—preserve direction and wording unless asked to change

## Example

```tsx
'use client';

import { useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import type { RootState } from '@/store/store';

export default function Example() {
  const items = useSelector((s: RootState) => s.weeklyTasks.tasks);
  const visible = useMemo(() => items?.filter(Boolean) ?? [], [items]);
  const onAction = useCallback(() => { /* ... */ }, []);
  return <div className="p-4">{/* ... */}</div>;
}
```
